[b]Requires the Odyssey expansion.[/b] The outfit stand this mod builds on is Odyssey content, so without it nothing happens. Harmony is also required.

In a game with so many choices of arms, armor, and apparel, why limit yourself to just one set for all jobs?  There is different gear best for work, play, combat - use all of them!

With Shift Change, colonists can change into the right clothes for what they are going to do, whether to work, to enjoy themselves, or to sleep, and back again afterwards.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-what-it-does.png[/img]

[h3]Indoors[/h3]

Your doctor operates in combat armor. It's always been on, and never taken off.

Put scrubs on a stand in the hospital. Anyone doing doctoring as [b]automatic[/b] work changes there first and changes back on the way out. The stand reads its room, so there is nothing to assign.

[img]https://i.imgur.com/flyDb1M.gif[/img]

Your space marine has been sleeping in their cataphract armor since the day you got it.

A bedroom stand hands out sleepwear at bedtime and holds their day clothes until morning. Set it to [b]Deposit only[/b], with its storage filter narrowed to the armor, and it parks the armor instead.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/demo-sleep.gif[/img]

Somewhere in your stockpile is probably not a set of formal wear that nobody has ever put on.  So go make some, and put them in the rec room.

Guests change as they arrive and change back when they leave.

[img]https://i.imgur.com/QgM2QRr.gif[/img]

[h3]Outdoors[/h3]

A stand can serve a radius around itself or an allowed area you paint, out in the open or across several rooms.

Builders now change before fetching their first load, when one area covers the stockpile and the site.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/demo-construction.gif[/img]

Wardens now change in the corridor and keep the uniform on in every cell.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/demo-prison.gif[/img]

Farmhands now change in the farmhouse and stay dressed for every field the area covers.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/demo-farm.gif[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-how-it-works.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/card-gizmos.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/card-stand-controls.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-limits.png[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Drinking and drug-taking do not count[/b], because fetching a beer is the same job in a bar or a corridor. Sitting down to socialize at a table [i]is[/i] caught, drink and all.
[*][b]Reading is left alone[/b], because a colonist picks their reading spot after setting off.
[*][b]Outdoors needs a radius or an allowed area.[/b] All open ground is one map-spanning room, so a stand out there serving its room serves nothing.
[*][b]Fetching building materials dresses nobody[/b], unless one allowed area covers both the stockpile and the site. Otherwise the builder changes at the frame, and keeps the hardhat on for the next load while its site is inside the stand's room, ring or area.
[*][b]Nobody is pulled out of bed[/b]: vanilla gives patients recreation they can take lying down, so they stay put.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-compatibility.png[/img]

You will run out of things to put on these stands almost immediately.

The base game has no scrubs and no chef's whites, and the one lab coat it does have is Anomaly's, so there is very little that says what a colonist actually does. Any apparel mod fixes that. [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1814987817]Vanilla Apparel Expanded[/url] adds all three and is what every screenshot here uses. Not affiliated with the Vanilla Expanded team.

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3792795811]Apparel Painter[/url], by the same author, was built for the wardrobe wall this mod ends up creating. It recolors apparel on the stands themselves, one garment or the whole stand at once, previewed live on the map. Bulk repainting tools cannot see inside a stand at all.

Known to work with:

[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=3545172389]Outfit Stands Plus[/url], in either load order. Its mechanized and mending stands are full shift stands. Every stand has one owner list, set with this mod's Set owner, and Outfit Stands Plus follows it: a stand with exactly one owner gives that colonist the Outfit Stands Plus button for it.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3717051546]Gerrymon's Hotspring Expanded[/url], with no setup at all. Its pool rooms turn a stand on for recreation by themselves.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2205980094]Standalone Hot Spring[/url], and any other modded recreation carrying a joy kind, though its room takes the switch by hand.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1127530465]Dubs Rimatomics[/url]. A reactor core, the plutonium processor or the spent fuel pool turns a stand on for fuel work by itself. Put a stand where the rods are kept as well as in the hall, since a colonist changes where the job begins. Working the console is not covered, being an order you give rather than a job.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-faq.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/card-faq.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beverage/shift-change/main/media/cards/banner-source.png[/img]

Automated test cases run inside RimWorld itself before every release, concentrated on what is hard to undo: a gravship flight, a colonist dying or being banished mid-shift, a save reloaded while someone is still in uniform. That does not make it bug-free. It means a failure in those paths shows up in testing, not in your save.

MIT licensed, with the design notes and the suite in the repository. No clothing, no buildings, no textures; it adds behavior to a building the game already draws. Written with AI assistance. No generated art anywhere.

[url=https://github.com/beverage/shift-change]github.com/beverage/shift-change[/url]

[url=https://github.com/aedbia/AutomaticSwapForStand]Automatic Swap Outfit[/url] by aedbia (MIT) covers adjacent ground, triggered solely by allowed-area boundaries.
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3237638097]Reel's Expanded Storage[/url] by Reel, for letting me use it for the shots above.

